{"type":"text","timestamp":1778456436952,"sessionID":"ses_1ebbc6de7ffe2IckJYD3NFv35z","part":{"id":"prt_e14439c8f001pQ3fRtcJFEPCK3","messageID":"msg_e144392cc001NeSMGeDtxzm1NE","sessionID":"ses_1ebbc6de7ffe2IckJYD3NFv35z","type":"text","text":"I'll work on this proof. The key insight is that if `u` tends to `l`, then `u ∘ φ` also tends to `l` when `φ` is strictly monotone. Mathlib has `Filter.Tendsto.comp` and `StrictMono.tendsto_atTop`.","time":{"start":1778456435855,"end":1778456436951}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778456441486,"sessionID":"ses_1ebbc6de7ffe2IckJYD3NFv35z","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"lean-checker_check_lean_proof","callID":"toolu_01Bn44yzUvEdxyCQfJbrVGjq","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"code":"import Mathlib\n\ntheorem subsequence_has_same_limit\n    {α : Type*} [TopologicalSpace α] {u : ℕ → α} {l : α}\n    (hu : Filter.Tendsto u Filter.atTop (nhds l)) :\n    ∀ φ : ℕ → ℕ, StrictMono φ →\n      ∃ m : α, Filter.Tendsto (fun n => u (φ n)) Filter.atTop (nhds m) ∧ m = l := by\n  intro φ hφ\n  refine ⟨l, ?_, rfl⟩\n  exact hu.comp hφ.tendsto_atTop"},"output":"{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"calls_used\": 1,\n  \"calls_budget\": 10,\n  \"lean_compiles\": true,\n  \"placeholder_violation\": false,\n  \"diagnostics\": []\n}","metadata":{"truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1778456438511,"end":1778456441484},"attachments":[]},"metadata":{"anthropic":{"caller":{"type":"direct"}}},"id":"prt_e1443a0d8001riOsRyAv91SiV0","sessionID":"ses_1ebbc6de7ffe2IckJYD3NFv35z","messageID":"msg_e144392cc001NeSMGeDtxzm1NE"}}
